-10-14T01:09:48Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T01:09:48Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/hanbong5938/desktop-pet/releases/download/v0.4.2/DesktopPet-v0.4.2-rig-native.json"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hanbong5938/desktop-pet/releases/assets/638775549","id":638775549,"node_id":"RA_kwDOVG1Ac84mEvD9","name":"SHA256SUMS","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":299,"digest":"sha256:2f807f9a2e48d32cf8f962b0ef5de7d39e7e0f32470cee45d3d4b208c917af85","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T01:09:48Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T01:09:48Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/hanbong5938/desktop-pet/releases/download/v0.4.2/SHA256SUMS"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hanbong5938/desktop-pet/tarball/v0.4.2","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hanbong5938/desktop-pet/zipball/v0.4.2","body":"# Desktop Pet v0.4.2 release notes\n\n## Publication boundary\n\nThe user approved separate **Core v0.4.2 and Herdr integration v0.4.1**, preserving every previously published tag/asset, after the bridge's strict public-tree gate exposed a Herdr publication error. **v0.4.2 is not yet published.** No future release ID, source revision or archive/installer digest is claimed. Valid published Core v0.4.0/v0.4.1 and Tern v0.2.0 remain immutable.\n\n## Problem and correction\n\nPublished Herdr integration v0.4.0, source `f65f123e17822ad838dd40a565900aca6347cd97`, release `412221638`, accidentally contained the generated legacy `dist/HerdrDesktopPet.app` tree in Git, despite its GitHub Release having no uploaded native assets. The thin integration filesystem/staging gates omitted `dist`, so they did not prove an integration-only published source closure. This was a publication error, not a user's host or account failure. Actual bridge build [38490571511](https://github.com/hanbong5938/desktop-pet/actions/runs/38490571511) rejected the real immutable public tree before building a bridge. No bridge was published and no legacy formula was changed by that failed run.\n\nThe correction removes that generated distribution from Herdr default source and makes both filesystem and tracked/source-tree ownership gates reject native/common product artifacts before publication. Herdr v0.4.0's public tag/body is retained as faulty history, never silently moved or overwritten. A new Herdr v0.4.1 is required for corrected managed migration. Core's immutable managed-retirement validation and bridge build authority cleanly move to that corrected integration ref; no old/new shim or relaxed artifact check is introduced.\n\nCore v0.4.2 remains the one common app/helper implementation. The genuine legacy bridge stays product **0.3.7**, protocol **3** / observation capability **1**, built from the exact newly published Core v0.4.2 source with the actual published Herdr v0.4.1 retirement ref. The neutral pair stays protocol **4** / observation capability **2** / integration API **1**. Integration versions are independent from the product version.\n\n## Observed corrective source checks\n\nThe new Herdr gate first rejected the real old `f65f123` tree on `dist/HerdrDesktopPet.app.rig-native.json`. Whole-index checking additionally exposed six tracked files from an earlier failed relative-path regression fixture, including a symlink and private test profile/locks; those generated test artifacts were removed, not confused with actual host evidence. Corrected integration source `2a1dae743c2a67659e8a6782eff9a11714a31837` was published to its adapter branch only, and the neutral app pins that exact clean source. It is not yet the corrected integration release/default consumer.\n\nAn independent anonymous Git clone of that public corrected source passed archived-tree and source/index guards. In that disposable clone, adding the **actual published native rig worker** as a renamed tracked text file absent from the filesystem failed the native-byte predicate; adding the actual historical symlink blob as an index-only regular-looking filename failed the regular Git-source predicate. Removing only those smoke index entries restored a passing source guard. A larger renamed actual native executable was also rejected at the bounded blob-read boundary. No fabricated host, release metadata or source-tree receipt was used.\n\nThe composed corrected Core working tree passed **741 Rust tests**, **62 Bun tests** and TypeScript with the exact new public adapter pin. Clean exact-source release packaging/signatures/public bytes remain a separate gate, not inferred from these tests. The current Wiki renderer generated **36 managed pages** after root-case repair; that local render is not successful Wiki publication.\n\n## Required independent checks\n\n- Corrected Herdr filesystem and actual immutable Git tree contain no common app/dist/native/artwork/rig closure; stage overlays and ignore rules cannot hide a tracked artifact.\n- Reuse real release metadata and authenticated installer bytes only after Core v0.4.2 is published. Existing Core v0.4.1 evidence is historical, not a fabricated future pin.\n- Run corrected gates, clean exact-source packaging, strict signatures and deployed closure, then anonymously verify every actual public asset.\n- Exercise real public formula/standalone/consumer installation and migration separately. Retain Stop/Unknown/no-replay safeguards and all legacy fault evidence.\n\nEarlier v0.4.1 actual publication, Brew/native readiness, config-wide owner regression, zero/Tern-only composition and original host-manager durable action evidence remain in the [v0.4.1 ledger](https://github.com/hanbong5938/desktop-pet/blob/main/docs/releases/v0.4.1.md). They do not establish this corrective release's future public bytes, corrected managed retirement or complete two-host delivery. Tern's real keychain/provider prerequisites remain blocked; no account, SDK receipt or transcript is fabricated. Wiki/Pages hosting and the final acceptance matrix remain separately verified.\n"}